  "id": "DrugBank_DB00620 - MONDO_grouped_9691_15821_45071",
  "verbalization": "Tiamcinolone, a corticosteroid, is linked to Mycosis Fungoides And Variants through a chain of indications involving Hydrocortisone Acetate. This relationship is supported by the shared use of Hydrocortisone Acetate in the treatment of Stevens-Johnson Syndrome, Sarcoidosis, and Renin-Angiotensin-Aldosterone System-blocker-induced Angioedema. These conditions, in turn, are associated with Mycosis Fungoides And Variants, suggesting a potential pathway where corticosteroids may influence immune-mediated disorders. The evidence implies that Triamcinolone could be repurposed for Mycosis Fungoides And Variants, possibly through mechanisms involving immune modulation or anti-inflammatory effects. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of corticosteroids in immune-related diseases, underscoring the potential for therapeutic repurposing in this context.",
